					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-438190#post-1362762</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-438190/scripture#post-1362762</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 01 Feb 2012 02:40:31 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Eskobar</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1173523</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Basically this. This uses a lot of the same kind of language as the COG, including the &quot;broken God&quot; line, but there's no connection there. The core of this is a story about making people into what you want them to be regardless of what they really are. The latter being humans, and the former being &quot;horrible fleshy Voltron-like abominations.&quot;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-438190#post-1362744</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-438190/scripture#post-1362744</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 01 Feb 2012 02:08:07 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Uncandescent</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>588650</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The way I read it, it sent out a signal to gather a bunch of humans together and tried to fuse them back into the form of the Great One at the behest of the dark voice. So now, they just have a gaint hunk of humans bonded together in a horrible fleshy Voltron-like abomination that is quite dead due to the general inability of humans to survive being combined into a horrible fleshy Voltron-like abomination.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
