					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-438190#post-1362639</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-438190/scripture#post-1362639</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 31 Jan 2012 22:59:50 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>MisterBibs</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>453823</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I actually think this is kinda sweet, if I'm remembering the SCP this is based of.</p> <p>The tower thinks humans are Gods, but is sad because we don't appreciate what it does in its love for us. Somehow, its convinced to build a New God. It's inert, but the Tower 'stands with it'. It has a God that does nothing, but the Tower is happy because its God is with it.</p> <p>I could be misinterpretating it.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
